[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186166904 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-83030669-b615-545c-b0dd-a292bd26151d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-83030669-b615-545c-b0dd-a292bd26151d" :question/id #uuid "83030669-b615-545c-b0dd-a292bd26151d" :question/math-academy-id "q-333014" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} & -\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}-6{t}^{2}+\\frac{41}{3}t-8 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-\\frac{13}{3}t+5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n    $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n    $\\,\\,{t}^{2}+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n    $\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n    {{field-2}}\n  </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n    .\n  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n    $-2$\n  </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-6{t}^{2}+\\frac{41}{3}t-8 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-\\frac{13}{3}t+5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}{t}^{2}+{b}_{2}t+{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]{t}^{2}+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} & -\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}{t}^{2}+{b}_{2}t+{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6{t}^{2}+\\frac{41}{3}t-8 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-\\frac{13}{3}t+5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{5{a}_{1}-8{a}_{2}}{3}){t}^{2}+(\\frac{5{b}_{1}-8{b}_{2}}{3})t+(\\frac{5{c}_{1}-8{c}_{2}}{3}) \\\\ (\\frac{-4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}}{3}){t}^{2}+(\\frac{-4{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}}{3})t+(\\frac{-4{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}}{3})\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6{t}^{2}+\\frac{41}{3}t-8 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-\\frac{13}{3}t+5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0{t}^{2}+2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 0{t}^{2}+2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{5{a}_{1}-8{a}_{2}-18}{3}){t}^{2}+(\\frac{5{b}_{1}-8{b}_{2}+41}{3})t+(\\frac{5{c}_{1}-8{c}_{2}-24}{3}) \\\\ (\\frac{-4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}+9}{3}){t}^{2}+(\\frac{-4{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}-13}{3})t+(\\frac{-4{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+15}{3})\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding coefficients of like powers of $t,$ we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5{a}_{1}-8{a}_{2}-18}{3}=0 \\\\ \\frac{-4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}+9}{3}=0 \\\\ \\frac{5{b}_{1}-8{b}_{2}+41}{3}=2{a}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{-4{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}-13}{3}=2{a}_{2} \\\\ \\frac{5{c}_{1}-8{c}_{2}-24}{3}={b}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{-4{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+15}{3}={b}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first and second equations, we get\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=2,\\,{a}_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the second and third equations, and solving for ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=-1,\\,{b}_{2}=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these last two values into the fourth and sixth equations, and solving for ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=1,\\,{c}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}-t+1 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+3t-2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{t}^{2}+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-68ebb6bc-8ecd-5644-95d4-7ec3ae49104a" "answer-field-ecb59f7c-3318-5766-b4e8-a59390b05bce" "answer-field-e2f40649-92a8-5fb9-9467-241241b205e5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-68ebb6bc-8ecd-5644-95d4-7ec3ae49104a" :answer-field/id #uuid "68ebb6bc-8ecd-5644-95d4-7ec3ae49104a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-93ad8973-8142-5ec3-9098-90c172b538cc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-93ad8973-8142-5ec3-9098-90c172b538cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93ad8973-8142-5ec3-9098-90c172b538cc" :answer/id #uuid "93ad8973-8142-5ec3-9098-90c172b538cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ecb59f7c-3318-5766-b4e8-a59390b05bce" :answer-field/id #uuid "ecb59f7c-3318-5766-b4e8-a59390b05bce" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c8b19b21-147d-5fdc-8f4d-a5e1d36c4409" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c8b19b21-147d-5fdc-8f4d-a5e1d36c4409"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8b19b21-147d-5fdc-8f4d-a5e1d36c4409" :answer/id #uuid "c8b19b21-147d-5fdc-8f4d-a5e1d36c4409" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e2f40649-92a8-5fb9-9467-241241b205e5" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2f40649-92a8-5fb9-9467-241241b205e5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2d3c4717-e0dc-535a-af6f-a87c7e67b231" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2d3c4717-e0dc-535a-af6f-a87c7e67b231"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d3c4717-e0dc-535a-af6f-a87c7e67b231" :answer/id #uuid "2d3c4717-e0dc-535a-af6f-a87c7e67b231" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166905 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e4dc2c43-c8eb-5bcf-a39b-abeb3bbb2764" "question-338f9068-6af3-5a99-af8d-48b1ac33890b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e4dc2c43-c8eb-5bcf-a39b-abeb3bbb2764" :question/id #uuid "e4dc2c43-c8eb-5bcf-a39b-abeb3bbb2764" :question/math-academy-id "q-333596" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t)+{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(0)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot {e}^{2(0)} \\\\ {e}^{2(0)}\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-0}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}+1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=3 \\\\ {c}_{2}+1=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we have ${c}_{1}=3.$ From the second equation, we get ${c}_{2}=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6da43cad-9102-5837-b0fd-1a8a586b0473" "answer-field-9d8e6467-de2d-5e39-8c4a-83e68c137488"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6da43cad-9102-5837-b0fd-1a8a586b0473" :answer-field/id #uuid "6da43cad-9102-5837-b0fd-1a8a586b0473" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-97a52fdf-3469-584f-9753-ff054f6fb144" :answer-field/choices ["answer-97a52fdf-3469-584f-9753-ff054f6fb144"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97a52fdf-3469-584f-9753-ff054f6fb144" :answer/id #uuid "97a52fdf-3469-584f-9753-ff054f6fb144" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9d8e6467-de2d-5e39-8c4a-83e68c137488" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d8e6467-de2d-5e39-8c4a-83e68c137488" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-bf902f7a-5b81-5b56-a8db-6e1126ebbd99" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bf902f7a-5b81-5b56-a8db-6e1126ebbd99"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf902f7a-5b81-5b56-a8db-6e1126ebbd99" :answer/id #uuid "bf902f7a-5b81-5b56-a8db-6e1126ebbd99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-338f9068-6af3-5a99-af8d-48b1ac33890b" :question/id #uuid "338f9068-6af3-5a99-af8d-48b1ac33890b" :question/math-academy-id "q-333610" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}-{t}^{2}+3t-2 \\\\ -4t+8\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-t+1 \\\\ 2t-3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-t+1 \\\\ 2t-3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{0} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{2(0)}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}-0+1 \\\\ 2(0)-3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+1 \\\\ {c}_{2}-3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+1=2 \\\\ {c}_{2}-3=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=1.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-t+1 \\\\ 2t-3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1a013588-c06c-5f55-940c-cbbd3057b90b" "answer-field-f188d9c6-552e-5855-a6ab-7fbed03f69d1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1a013588-c06c-5f55-940c-cbbd3057b90b" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a013588-c06c-5f55-940c-cbbd3057b90b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-388279d1-e34b-50a4-9ce3-cc8dace5482c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-388279d1-e34b-50a4-9ce3-cc8dace5482c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-388279d1-e34b-50a4-9ce3-cc8dace5482c" :answer/id #uuid "388279d1-e34b-50a4-9ce3-cc8dace5482c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f188d9c6-552e-5855-a6ab-7fbed03f69d1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f188d9c6-552e-5855-a6ab-7fbed03f69d1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8cfa8656-14de-5766-be79-8ae7b5309f14" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8cfa8656-14de-5766-be79-8ae7b5309f14"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8cfa8656-14de-5766-be79-8ae7b5309f14" :answer/id #uuid "8cfa8656-14de-5766-be79-8ae7b5309f14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-cd780238-6561-5335-8628-86c0ec2f992b" :activity/id #uuid "cd780238-6561-5335-8628-86c0ec2f992b" :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050801 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-b1481bb9-2ae6-5119-bb02-e73517637dbf" "step-8af18c3c-574b-5432-b3c3-e6d29db74282" "step-4b0c53fd-63dc-5e60-91b1-9c112e1416ed" "step-8300d53d-a4ca-5fa3-80df-bd513e8ce9c1" "step-97a61470-ffa2-5ca9-9f97-05f72a262645"] :activity/first-step "step-b1481bb9-2ae6-5119-bb02-e73517637dbf" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-b1481bb9-2ae6-5119-bb02-e73517637dbf" :step/id #uuid "b1481bb9-2ae6-5119-bb02-e73517637dbf" :step/content 17592186305112 :step/next "step-8af18c3c-574b-5432-b3c3-e6d29db74282" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8af18c3c-574b-5432-b3c3-e6d29db74282" :step/id #uuid "8af18c3c-574b-5432-b3c3-e6d29db74282" :step/content 17592186305149 :step/next "step-4b0c53fd-63dc-5e60-91b1-9c112e1416ed" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4b0c53fd-63dc-5e60-91b1-9c112e1416ed" :step/id #uuid "4b0c53fd-63dc-5e60-91b1-9c112e1416ed" :step/content "question-83030669-b615-545c-b0dd-a292bd26151d" :step/next "step-8300d53d-a4ca-5fa3-80df-bd513e8ce9c1" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8300d53d-a4ca-5fa3-80df-bd513e8ce9c1" :step/id #uuid "8300d53d-a4ca-5fa3-80df-bd513e8ce9c1" :step/content "question-e4dc2c43-c8eb-5bcf-a39b-abeb3bbb2764" :step/next "step-97a61470-ffa2-5ca9-9f97-05f72a262645" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-97a61470-ffa2-5ca9-9f97-05f72a262645" :step/id #uuid "97a61470-ffa2-5ca9-9f97-05f72a262645" :step/content "question-338f9068-6af3-5a99-af8d-48b1ac33890b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-83030669-b615-545c-b0dd-a292bd26151d" :question/id #uuid "83030669-b615-545c-b0dd-a292bd26151d"] ["question-83030669-b615-545c-b0dd-a292bd26151d" :question/math-academy-id "q-333014"] ["question-83030669-b615-545c-b0dd-a292bd26151d" :question/problem "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} & -\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}-6{t}^{2}+\\frac{41}{3}t-8 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-\\frac{13}{3}t+5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n    $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n    $\\,\\,{t}^{2}+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n    $\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n    {{field-2}}\n  </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n    .\n  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n    $-2$\n  </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] ["question-83030669-b615-545c-b0dd-a292bd26151d" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-6{t}^{2}+\\frac{41}{3}t-8 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-\\frac{13}{3}t+5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}{t}^{2}+{b}_{2}t+{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]{t}^{2}+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} & -\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}{t}^{2}+{b}_{2}t+{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6{t}^{2}+\\frac{41}{3}t-8 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-\\frac{13}{3}t+5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{5{a}_{1}-8{a}_{2}}{3}){t}^{2}+(\\frac{5{b}_{1}-8{b}_{2}}{3})t+(\\frac{5{c}_{1}-8{c}_{2}}{3}) \\\\ (\\frac{-4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}}{3}){t}^{2}+(\\frac{-4{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}}{3})t+(\\frac{-4{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}}{3})\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6{t}^{2}+\\frac{41}{3}t-8 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-\\frac{13}{3}t+5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0{t}^{2}+2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 0{t}^{2}+2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{5{a}_{1}-8{a}_{2}-18}{3}){t}^{2}+(\\frac{5{b}_{1}-8{b}_{2}+41}{3})t+(\\frac{5{c}_{1}-8{c}_{2}-24}{3}) \\\\ (\\frac{-4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}+9}{3}){t}^{2}+(\\frac{-4{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}-13}{3})t+(\\frac{-4{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+15}{3})\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding coefficients of like powers of $t,$ we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5{a}_{1}-8{a}_{2}-18}{3}=0 \\\\ \\frac{-4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}+9}{3}=0 \\\\ \\frac{5{b}_{1}-8{b}_{2}+41}{3}=2{a}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{-4{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}-13}{3}=2{a}_{2} \\\\ \\frac{5{c}_{1}-8{c}_{2}-24}{3}={b}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{-4{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+15}{3}={b}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first and second equations, we get\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=2,\\,{a}_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the second and third equations, and solving for ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=-1,\\,{b}_{2}=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these last two values into the fourth and sixth equations, and solving for ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=1,\\,{c}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}-t+1 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+3t-2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{t}^{2}+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"] ["question-83030669-b615-545c-b0dd-a292bd26151d" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-68ebb6bc-8ecd-5644-95d4-7ec3ae49104a" :answer-field/id #uuid "68ebb6bc-8ecd-5644-95d4-7ec3ae49104a"] ["answer-93ad8973-8142-5ec3-9098-90c172b538cc" :answer/id #uuid "93ad8973-8142-5ec3-9098-90c172b538cc"] ["answer-93ad8973-8142-5ec3-9098-90c172b538cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-93ad8973-8142-5ec3-9098-90c172b538cc" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-field-68ebb6bc-8ecd-5644-95d4-7ec3ae49104a" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-68ebb6bc-8ecd-5644-95d4-7ec3ae49104a" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-68ebb6bc-8ecd-5644-95d4-7ec3ae49104a" :answer-field/correct "answer-93ad8973-8142-5ec3-9098-90c172b538cc"] ["answer-field-68ebb6bc-8ecd-5644-95d4-7ec3ae49104a" :answer-field/choices "answer-93ad8973-8142-5ec3-9098-90c172b538cc"] ["answer-field-ecb59f7c-3318-5766-b4e8-a59390b05bce" :answer-field/id #uuid "ecb59f7c-3318-5766-b4e8-a59390b05bce"] ["answer-c8b19b21-147d-5fdc-8f4d-a5e1d36c4409" :answer/id #uuid "c8b19b21-147d-5fdc-8f4d-a5e1d36c4409"] ["answer-c8b19b21-147d-5fdc-8f4d-a5e1d36c4409" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c8b19b21-147d-5fdc-8f4d-a5e1d36c4409" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-field-ecb59f7c-3318-5766-b4e8-a59390b05bce" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-ecb59f7c-3318-5766-b4e8-a59390b05bce" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-ecb59f7c-3318-5766-b4e8-a59390b05bce" :answer-field/correct "answer-c8b19b21-147d-5fdc-8f4d-a5e1d36c4409"] ["answer-field-ecb59f7c-3318-5766-b4e8-a59390b05bce" :answer-field/choices "answer-c8b19b21-147d-5fdc-8f4d-a5e1d36c4409"] ["answer-field-e2f40649-92a8-5fb9-9467-241241b205e5" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2f40649-92a8-5fb9-9467-241241b205e5"] ["answer-2d3c4717-e0dc-535a-af6f-a87c7e67b231" :answer/id #uuid "2d3c4717-e0dc-535a-af6f-a87c7e67b231"] ["answer-2d3c4717-e0dc-535a-af6f-a87c7e67b231" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2d3c4717-e0dc-535a-af6f-a87c7e67b231" :answer/value "3"] ["answer-field-e2f40649-92a8-5fb9-9467-241241b205e5" :answer-field/key "field-3"] ["answer-field-e2f40649-92a8-5fb9-9467-241241b205e5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-e2f40649-92a8-5fb9-9467-241241b205e5" :answer-field/correct "answer-2d3c4717-e0dc-535a-af6f-a87c7e67b231"] ["answer-field-e2f40649-92a8-5fb9-9467-241241b205e5" :answer-field/choices "answer-2d3c4717-e0dc-535a-af6f-a87c7e67b231"] ["question-83030669-b615-545c-b0dd-a292bd26151d" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-68ebb6bc-8ecd-5644-95d4-7ec3ae49104a"] ["question-83030669-b615-545c-b0dd-a292bd26151d" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-ecb59f7c-3318-5766-b4e8-a59390b05bce"] ["question-83030669-b615-545c-b0dd-a292bd26151d" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-e2f40649-92a8-5fb9-9467-241241b205e5"] [17592186166904 :knowledge-point/questions "question-83030669-b615-545c-b0dd-a292bd26151d"] ["question-e4dc2c43-c8eb-5bcf-a39b-abeb3bbb2764" :question/id #uuid "e4dc2c43-c8eb-5bcf-a39b-abeb3bbb2764"] ["question-e4dc2c43-c8eb-5bcf-a39b-abeb3bbb2764" :question/math-academy-id "q-333596"] ["question-e4dc2c43-c8eb-5bcf-a39b-abeb3bbb2764" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t)+{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$"] ["question-e4dc2c43-c8eb-5bcf-a39b-abeb3bbb2764" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(0)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot {e}^{2(0)} \\\\ {e}^{2(0)}\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-0}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}+1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=3 \\\\ {c}_{2}+1=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we have ${c}_{1}=3.$ From the second equation, we get ${c}_{2}=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"] ["question-e4dc2c43-c8eb-5bcf-a39b-abeb3bbb2764" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-6da43cad-9102-5837-b0fd-1a8a586b0473" :answer-field/id #uuid "6da43cad-9102-5837-b0fd-1a8a586b0473"] ["answer-97a52fdf-3469-584f-9753-ff054f6fb144" :answer/id #uuid "97a52fdf-3469-584f-9753-ff054f6fb144"] ["answer-97a52fdf-3469-584f-9753-ff054f6fb144" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-97a52fdf-3469-584f-9753-ff054f6fb144" :answer/value "3"] ["answer-field-6da43cad-9102-5837-b0fd-1a8a586b0473" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-6da43cad-9102-5837-b0fd-1a8a586b0473" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-6da43cad-9102-5837-b0fd-1a8a586b0473" :answer-field/correct "answer-97a52fdf-3469-584f-9753-ff054f6fb144"] ["answer-field-6da43cad-9102-5837-b0fd-1a8a586b0473" :answer-field/choices "answer-97a52fdf-3469-584f-9753-ff054f6fb144"] ["answer-field-9d8e6467-de2d-5e39-8c4a-83e68c137488" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d8e6467-de2d-5e39-8c4a-83e68c137488"] ["answer-bf902f7a-5b81-5b56-a8db-6e1126ebbd99" :answer/id #uuid "bf902f7a-5b81-5b56-a8db-6e1126ebbd99"] ["answer-bf902f7a-5b81-5b56-a8db-6e1126ebbd99" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-bf902f7a-5b81-5b56-a8db-6e1126ebbd99" :answer/value "3"] ["answer-field-9d8e6467-de2d-5e39-8c4a-83e68c137488" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-9d8e6467-de2d-5e39-8c4a-83e68c137488" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-9d8e6467-de2d-5e39-8c4a-83e68c137488" :answer-field/correct "answer-bf902f7a-5b81-5b56-a8db-6e1126ebbd99"] ["answer-field-9d8e6467-de2d-5e39-8c4a-83e68c137488" :answer-field/choices "answer-bf902f7a-5b81-5b56-a8db-6e1126ebbd99"] ["question-e4dc2c43-c8eb-5bcf-a39b-abeb3bbb2764" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-6da43cad-9102-5837-b0fd-1a8a586b0473"] ["question-e4dc2c43-c8eb-5bcf-a39b-abeb3bbb2764" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-9d8e6467-de2d-5e39-8c4a-83e68c137488"] [17592186166905 :knowledge-point/questions "question-e4dc2c43-c8eb-5bcf-a39b-abeb3bbb2764"] ["question-338f9068-6af3-5a99-af8d-48b1ac33890b" :question/id #uuid "338f9068-6af3-5a99-af8d-48b1ac33890b"] ["question-338f9068-6af3-5a99-af8d-48b1ac33890b" :question/math-academy-id "q-333610"] ["question-338f9068-6af3-5a99-af8d-48b1ac33890b" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}-{t}^{2}+3t-2 \\\\ -4t+8\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-t+1 \\\\ 2t-3\\end{aligned}].$"] ["question-338f9068-6af3-5a99-af8d-48b1ac33890b" :question/worked-solution "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-t+1 \\\\ 2t-3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{0} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{2(0)}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}-0+1 \\\\ 2(0)-3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+1 \\\\ {c}_{2}-3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+1=2 \\\\ {c}_{2}-3=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=1.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-t+1 \\\\ 2t-3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"] ["question-338f9068-6af3-5a99-af8d-48b1ac33890b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-1a013588-c06c-5f55-940c-cbbd3057b90b" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a013588-c06c-5f55-940c-cbbd3057b90b"] ["answer-388279d1-e34b-50a4-9ce3-cc8dace5482c" :answer/id #uuid "388279d1-e34b-50a4-9ce3-cc8dace5482c"] ["answer-388279d1-e34b-50a4-9ce3-cc8dace5482c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-388279d1-e34b-50a4-9ce3-cc8dace5482c" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-field-1a01358